 its deepest. Daily price ranges tightened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On May 3, 2021 it closed at $35.54, its first close above the base high of $35.17. Volume that day was 2.9M shares, 1.69x the prior 10-day average of 1.7M. It held, never closing below the level three days running, reached a best close of $48.96, and the chart ends at $45.71.","lesson":"This is an example of a textbook breakout: a base, then a close above it on heavy volume, and it held. This is the pattern the rules are built around."}}